  "name": "Menacing Attack",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/melee/hand-grip-hammer-spiked-blue.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you hit a creature with an attack roll, you can expend one Superiority Die to attempt to frighten the target. Add the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition until the end of your next turn.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-sPNAs2sYsogCvvxn\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>This feature includes a <strong>Strength Save</strong> activity and a <strong>Dexterity Save</strong> activity which will consume a use of your Superiority Die.</p><p>The <strong>Damage</strong> activity allows you to select the type of damage it should deal in the roll dialog.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
